{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1343548-quality-question","id":1343548,"title":"Quality Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-25T02:23:37-07:00","id":1343548,"title":"Quality Question","content":"Hi.<br /> I have a question about the quality of hard copies of the M20 book. I have it on PDF, but I think I would prefer hard copy if I was running a game rather than just a player character. So I was looking on DrivethruRPG and contemplating the standard color or premium color. I was checking into reviews, and I read many distressing reports about poor quality binding. Like, really bad.<br /> <br /> So I am seeking advice from anyone who has a hard copy. How bad is it? Am I better off just sticking with the PDF? I have PDFs of the other M20 books as well. If I were to get a hard copy of just one, which would be the better choice? Or am I better off just printing reference pages?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T10:17:35-07:00","id":1343607,"title":"","content":"...yeaaaaahhhh...<br /> <br /> I started using my regular copy in a chronicle I'm in...and it didn't take long for the thing to fall apart. Was forced to cobble together the money I had to buy one of the overstocked Deluxe copies on IPR as a replacement, just to future proof it from falling apart again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T10:45:55-07:00","id":1343610,"title":"","content":"Does the deluxe hold up better? I am looking at a price difference of 35 bucks (65 for the regular, 100 for the deluxe). I saw a premium leather bound version on ebay for 300, and I just don't need the book that badly.<br /> <br /> What if I just got Book of Secrets? I have the PDFs and a laptop. I have hard copy of Sorcerers Crusade and the guy I game with has *all* the old books in hard copy (I have most of them, again on PDF). I suppose that is a matter of personal preference. What is the quality like on *that* book? How often do you refer to it? Is it used regular, or as a one and done for building characters?<br /> <br /> As a side note, of the M20 core books I have in PDF, I like Gods &amp; Monsters the best. But it is not essential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T11:17:46-07:00","id":1343611,"title":"","content":"Oh, by &quot;deluxe&quot; version I meant <a href=\"https://www.indiepressrevolution.com/xcart/Mage-The-Ascension-20th-Anniversary-Edition-Deluxe.html\" target=\"_blank\">THIS one. </a><br /> <br /> Honestly the issue doesn't have to do with the quality of the binding so much as it does with the page count. It's a +700 page book that is very heavy, while the other PoD books typically bind 200-400 page books.<br /> <br /> PDFs alone are still doable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T08:03:13-07:00","id":1343766,"title":"","content":"Just use PDFs - the quickstart guide PDF contains most of what you'll need, and you can always print out a cheap black and white copy... you do own the PDF, so making a printed version seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T10:12:34-08:00","id":1345607,"title":"","content":"My copies of mage the ascension is still in the original shrinkwrap. I bought two of the deluxe kickstarter copies.<br /> <br /> I have started using of my Exalted 3E deluxe corebooks, which are of similiar size. They are holding up reasonably well after some light use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T10:13:19-08:00","id":1345608,"title":"","content":"Also, the core M:tA20 book is so... verbose that much of what you need can be cobbled together from the PDF with a splitter program and printed off seperately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}